            <animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="translate"
                values="0 24; 0 -20" dur="2.4s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="0s"/>
        </g>
        <g>
            <line x1="60" y1="0" x2="60" y2="8"/>
            <line x1="56" y1="4" x2="64" y2="4"/>
            <animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;1;0" dur="2.4s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="0.6s"/>
            <animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="translate"
                values="0 24; 0 -20" dur="2.4s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="0.6s"/>
        </g>
        <g>
            <line x1="76" y1="0" x2="76" y2="8"/>
            <line x1="72" y1="4" x2="80" y2="4"/>
            <animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;1;0" dur="2.4s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="1.2s"/>
            <animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="translate"
                values="0 24; 0 -20" dur="2.4s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="1.2s"/>
        </g>
        <g>
            <line x1="52" y1="0" x2="52" y2="6"/>
            <line x1="49" y1="3" x2="55" y2="3"/>
            <animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;1;0" dur="2.4s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="1.8s"/>
            <animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="translate"
                values="0 24; 0 -20" dur="2.4s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="1.8s"/>
        </g>
        <g>
            <line x1="68" y1="0" x2="68" y2="6"/>
            <line x1="65" y1="3" x2="71" y2="3"/>
            <animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;1;0" dur="2.4s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="0.9s"/>
            <animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="translate"
                values="0 24; 0 -20" dur="2.4s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="0.9s"/>
        </g>
    </g>
</svg>
                </div>
                <div class="eco-body">
                    <span class="eco-tag">In vivo</span>
                    <h3>Physiological</h3>
                    <p>Protocols are evaluated against animal model studies and human trial data. Where the model predicts an outcome, that outcome is checked against published physiological responses.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Animal disease models</strong> — established systems</li>
                        <li><strong>Clinical trial data</strong> — dosing, outcomes, events</li>
                        <li><strong>Human cohorts</strong> — time-to-response</li>
                        <li><strong>Longitudinal outcomes</strong> — durability at follow-up</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cross-cut">
            <h3>How we know it holds</h3>
            <div class="cross-grid">

                <div class="cross-item">
                    <div class="cross-icon">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" width="44" height="44" fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" class="icon-leaf">
                            <path d="M32 56 L32 20"/>
                            <path d="M32 20 L18 8"/>
                            <path d="M32 20 L46 8"/>
                            <path d="M32 36 L20 26"/>
                            <path d="M32 36 L44 26"/>
                            <circle cx="18" cy="8" r="3" class="icon-dot" fill="#a7f3d0" stroke="none"/>
                            <circle cx="46" cy="8" r="3" class="icon-dot" fill="#a7f3d0" stroke="none" style="animation-delay:-0.5s"/>
                            <circle cx="20" cy="26" r="2.6" class="icon-dot" fill="#a7f3d0" stroke="none" style="animation-delay:-1s"/>
                            <circle cx="44" cy="26" r="2.6" class="icon-dot" fill="#a7f3d0" stroke="none" style="animation-delay:-1.5s"/>
                            <circle cx="32" cy="56" r="3" class="icon-dot" fill="#34d399" stroke="none" style="animation-delay:-2s"/>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cross-title">Cross-species</div>
                    <div class="cross-desc">A pattern that holds across evolutionary distance is a pattern worth trusting.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="cross-item">
                    <div class="cross-icon">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" width="44" height="44" fill="none" stroke="#a7f3d0" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" class="icon-leaf">
                            <ellipse cx="32" cy="42" rx="14" ry="11" class="icon-pulse"/>
                            <circle cx="20" cy="24" r="5"/>
                            <circle cx="30" cy="19" r="5"/>
                            <circle cx="40" cy="20" r="5"/>
                            <circle cx="48" cy="28" r="4.5"/>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cross-title">Animal models</div>
                    <div class="cross-desc">Nothing reaches a human until it holds in a living organism first.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="cross-item">
                    <div class="cross-icon">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" width="44" height="44" fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" class="icon-leaf">
                            <circle cx="32" cy="16" r="6" class="icon-pulse"/>
                            <path d="M32 24 L32 44"/>
                            <path d="M18 32 L46 32"/>
                            <path d="M32 44 L22 58"/>
                            <path d="M32 44 L42 58"/>
                            <circle cx="32" cy="16" r="2" class="icon-dot" fill="#a7f3d0" stroke="none"/>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cross-title">Human trials</div>
                    <div class="cross-desc">The final check. If a protocol works in people, everything beneath it was correct.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="cross-item">
                    <div class="cross-icon">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" width="44" height="44" fill="none" stroke="#a7f3d0" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" class="icon-leaf">
                            <path d="M14 14 L50 14 L38 32 L38 50 L26 50 L26 32 Z" class="icon-pulse"/>
                            <circle cx="20" cy="22" r="2" class="icon-dot" fill="#4ade80" stroke="none"/>
                            <circle cx="32" cy="24" r="2" class="icon-dot" fill="#4ade80" stroke="none" style="animation-delay:-0.4s"/>
                            <circle cx="44" cy="22" r="2" class="icon-dot" fill="#4ade80" stroke="none" style="animation-delay:-0.8s"/>
                            <circle cx="32" cy="44" r="2.4" class="icon-dot" fill="#a7f3d0" stroke="none" style="animation-delay:-1.2s"/>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cross-title">Held-out first</div>
                    <div class="cross-desc">Nothing reaches a mouse until it passes on data the model has never seen.</div>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="different">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Most tools solve <span class="accent">one piece</span>.<br>GAIA runs the whole chain — and then goes further.</h2>

        <div class="movements">

            <div class="movement">
                <div class="movement-mark">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="40" height="40">
                        <path d="M 2 20 Q 8 8 14 20 T 26 20 T 38 20"
                              fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round">
                            <animate attributeName="stroke-dasharray" values="0 200;200 0" dur="4s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </path>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="movement-body">
                    <h3>It reads the genome <em>backward</em>.</h3>
                    <p>Standard pipelines pick a target, then ask which variants matter. GAIA starts from the raw genome and the patient's own symptom pattern, and works back to the genes actually producing the disease. Nothing is hand-coded. Everything is derived.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="movement">
                <div class="movement-mark">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="40" height="40">
                        <path d="M 2 20 L 10 20 L 12 12 L 16 28 L 20 20 L 28 20 L 30 10 L 34 30 L 38 20"
                              fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <animate attributeName="stroke-dasharray" values="0 200;200 0" dur="4s" begin="1s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </path>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="movement-body">
                    <h3>It reawakens what disease <em>silences</em>.</h3>
                    <p>Disease doesn't just damage tissue — it shuts down the repair pathways that would heal it. GAIA identifies compounds that reactivate those silenced signals, the difference between managing a disease and reversing it.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="movement">
                <div class="movement-mark">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="40" height="40">
                        <path d="M 2 30 L 12 30 L 16 14 L 20 34 L 24 22 L 28 30 L 38 30"
                              fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <animate attributeName="stroke-dasharray" values="0 200;200 0" dur="4s" begin="2s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </path>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="movement-body">
                    <h3>It <em>reverses</em>, not just manages.</h3>
                    <p>The pathways that repair tissue are the same ones that repair DNA. When GAIA reawakens them, it does not stop at the joint — it reverses up to ten years of accumulated DNA-repair deficit in simulation. Reversal, not management.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="movement">
                <div class="movement-mark">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="40" height="40">
                        <path d="M 2 20 L 10 20 L 14 10 L 20 30 L 26 10 L 32 30 L 36 20 L 38 20"
                              fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <animate attributeName="stroke-dasharray" values="0 200;200 0" dur="4s" begin="3s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </path>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="movement-body">
                    <h3>It <em>checks itself</em> before it speaks.</h3>
                    <p>A claim that survives only computation is not a claim. It is a guess. Verification is not a phase — it runs alongside every prediction, and the results are published.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="movement">
                <div class="movement-mark">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="40" height="40">
                        <path d="M 2 20 L 12 20 L 16 12 L 20 28 L 24 12 L 28 28 L 32 20 L 38 20"
                              fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <animate attributeName="stroke-dasharray" values="0 200;200 0" dur="4s" begin="4s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </path>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="movement-body">
                    <h3>It has already <em>run once</em>.</h3>
                    <p>End to end, on Ankylosing Spondylitis. In simulation the full pipeline — genome read, variants mapped, compounds ranked, protocol designed — took BASDAI from 6.9 to 1.0 over 12 months. Clinical remission. The result, the numbers, and the method are public.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="sources">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>It reads the <span class="accent">open web</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">
            The system doesn't wait for someone to hand it data. It reads
            hundreds of curated, reputable URLs — peer-reviewed literature,
            reference genomes, protein structures, clinical registries — and
            grows as new findings are published.
        </p>

